body:
DEC03 proposes this addition to gpu/hwcodec/tests/hw/n2vc_hw_fake.{h,c}. It is 6 lines of state + one call site; nothing existing changes when the hook is not installed.

In n2vc_hw_fake.h:
  /* DEC03: optional register hook, called from fake_regs() for every READ/WRITE after the window/power/alignment
   * checks and before the default register array. Return 1 = handled (set *value for a read), 0 = default handling,
   * -errno = fail the op. Not called for WRITE_MASK or POLL (both are implemented as plain writes/reads by the fake;
   * if you prefer, fold them first). ctx is the caller pointer. */
  typedef int (*n2vc_hw_fake_reg_hook)(void *ctx, unsigned win, uint32_t off, int is_write, uint32_t *value);
  int n2vc_hw_fake_set_reg_hook(struct n2vc_hw *hw, n2vc_hw_fake_reg_hook fn, void *ctx);

In fake_regs(): for each op, after check_reg()/block_on() succeed and before the switch branch for READ/WRITE, if (f->hook) { int hr = f->hook(f->hook_ctx, o->window, o->offset, o->op == RWVC_OP_WRITE, &o->value); if (hr > 0) { record "R/W ... hook" (your recorder syntax, e.g. append " hook"); continue; } if (hr < 0) { rc = hr; break; } }

My side: n2vld_hook(ctx, win, off, write, value) handles win==RWVC_WIN_VDEC_VLD (off is relative to 0x16020000) and win==12 (proposed RWVC_WIN_VDEC_ALL, off relative to 0x16000000; DEC07/DEC04 are adding it) and returns 0 for every other window/offset, so the fake array keeps the SPS/PPS/status registers you already store. The model needs the bitstream bytes: it takes a struct n2vld_bus { int (*read_pa)(void *ctx, uint32_t pa, void *dst, uint32_t bytes); void *ctx; } at n2vld_create() time, so no PA->host function is needed from you. My tests drive the hook through a small wrapper around your fake, so I can land and test before you edit anything; when you add the setter, the integration is just n2vc_hw_fake_set_reg_hook(hw, n2vld_hook, vld).

If you would rather expose the hook as a field in a struct you already keep, or name it differently, send the exact text and I will use it. If you think the fake should own the AVC_VLD window (0x16022000) separately from DEC07's VDEC_ALL, say so; my hook accepts either, it only needs the window index and relative offset.
